{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod","id":1050549,"title":"My Dark god beats yours!:Who is the most evil one in WoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-17T09:41:02-08:00","id":1050549,"title":"My Dark god beats yours!:Who is the most evil one in WoD","content":"The Wyrm, Azura, The Grandma, The Weaver, Belial the Great Beast, God, The K'llashaa etc etc...<br /> <br /> Theres so many cosmic deities in the world of darkness that i wonder, who is the true evil?. and who could beat the living crap out of the other","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T13:24:01-08:00","id":1050682,"title":"","content":"Frankly I don't consider the Wyrm, the Weaver or Grandma evil. The former two are suffering from their own brands of insanity that's twisted what they were originally meant to be. And Grandma... well Grandma from the start does not understand the concept of life outside of herself. She's devouring the universe which she thinks is lifeless so that she can create her own universe with her creations in it. If the players manage to reach her and explain, she's actually shocked by what's she's doing.<br /> <br /> The K'llashaa, or at least the beings they serve, are utterly alien to humans and human morality. Does that make them evil? By human standards, yeah. But they are not human. They do not have human morality. They have their own morality, whatever it may be.<br /> <br /> God is God. He's bloodthirsty tyrant, a well-meaning asshole, a frantic being trying to keep universe together with ever-diminishing time and choices, the sinister puppetmaster that delights as the universe dances to his tune and suffers for him or all the above at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T13:43:38-08:00","id":1050691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1050682#post1050682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly I don't consider the Wyrm, the Weaver or Grandma evil. The former two are suffering from their own brands of insanity that's twisted what they were originally meant to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh... they get a pass on being evil just because they are insane? What. Most of the beings on this list are not capable of being 'sane' in any real sense of the word. I say judge these creatures by their actions, not by whatever unknowable state their mind might be be in.<br /> <br /> I say the Wyrm is the worst, mainly based on scope. It torments and corrupts across the world and beyond. Whole spirits and realms writhe in its cancerous grasp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T14:45:42-08:00","id":1050727,"title":"","content":"Belial is barely on the level of the others in that list. Sure, he's extremely powerful but he's powerful on a level that player characters can hypothetically deal with thim. The others? Not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T16:24:41-08:00","id":1050788,"title":"","content":"Evil is a human-level thing based on free will. The human-level agents of the Weaver and Wyrm are evil (whether you are talking about Technocrats and Drones or Nephandi and Fomori) because they have a choice in their actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T17:09:41-08:00","id":1050804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1050788#post1050788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evil is a human-level thing based on free will. The human-level agents of the Weaver and Wyrm are evil (whether you are talking about Technocrats and Drones or Nephandi and Fomori) because they have a choice in their actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technocrats aren't agents of the Weaver. Not like, say, Shinzui Industries or DNA, at any rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T19:16:32-08:00","id":1050846,"title":"","content":"Actually, according to the Book of the Weaver, they are even though they do not realize it. They are the perfect agents because their actions weaken the Wyld and Gaia, as well as strengthening the Weaver, and they do not request that much from the Weaver in exchange for their service because they actually think that they are creating a better world for humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T23:15:37-08:00","id":1051388,"title":"","content":"I'm convinced that Gaia is secretly the worst of all. I just can't accept Garou excuses enough to believe otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh","name":"Mr. Sluagh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T07:16:01-08:00","id":1051507,"title":"","content":"I imagine that some people are convinced that the mother of all is the worst of all. They must live in a dark world if they think that all life is basically evil. I do wonder what their hope for the future is though? That the Singularity will come and that our robot overlords will be merciful when they turn us into lubricant?<br /> <br /> Gain is Nature. Nature is neutral. Now, I know that some people have some prejudice against the Garou based on their previous posts, but I really do not see what is so awful about trying to preserve the biosphere from collapse. If the biosphere collapses, humanity dies along with everything else, so I think the Garou are doing humanity a favor by trying to save Gaia. And blaming modern Garou for the Wars of Rage are a bit like blaming modern Mongolians for Genghis Khan.<br /> <br /> The Garou try to save Gaia by sabotaging Pentex, but they try to change the behaviors of other human groups through a mixture of education, political action, and whistleblowing. While the Red Talons want to be more violent, they are the smallest tribe and will likely go extinct soon enough because they are unwilling to use the human world to save their Wolf Kinfolk. Compare that to the tactics of the Ratkin, who are planning of killing ninety percent of humanity through famine, plague, and war. <br /> <br /> The Garou are the friends of humanity when compared to the Ratkin and are the unsung saviors of humanity when compared to the rest of the supernatural creatures, who seem to seek to eat and/or enslave humanity. The Garou just want a stable biosphere on Earth so they can spend their lives interacting with the Middle Umbra. Heck, I imagine the majority of the Garou would be thrilled if they could get away with letting their Kinfolk deal with humanity on their behalf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T08:45:02-08:00","id":1051534,"title":"","content":"The Children seem pretty gosh-darn evil. They seemingly predate Vampirism, and yet they're sort of like Vampires since sunlight kills them. And waking them up or keeping them down is the prime motivation of two thirds of the Balli, and that makes them directly responsible for a tonne of evil shit.<br /> <br /> The Grand Maw isn't knowingly evil, but in terms of cosmic destruction she trumps everything else in the universe, since she is the patient force of undoing which will even devour the Wyrm once it's finished eating everything else.<br /> <br /> Satan, oddly enough, seems like a swell guy. And I actually quite like Lilith. Caine is a brooding idiot somewhat akin to an angry manchild, but he isn't evil.<br /> <br /> Kupala is A Bit Evil. He kind of corrupts everything he touches, hence the Tzimisce obsession with gore and ugliness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T12:03:10-08:00","id":1051600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Sluagh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1051388#post1051388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm convinced that Gaia is secretly the worst of all. I just can't accept Garou excuses enough to believe otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, even if some Garou go batshit and say that they're doing an atrocity in Gaia's name, Gaia didn't actually tell them to do it. They're just bringing human religious fervor into the mix, which is something that you actively have to do, rather than just having it fall out. Gaia doesn't really say or do much on a scale that anyone not also a cosmic being would see or comprehend. Even if she's lower than the Triat, that's still incomprehensibly huge, and her avatar would need and avatar and its avatar would need an avatar to talk to people in vague terms, which doesn't really happen very often.<br /> <br /> Now, when it comes to the purpose of some Fera, you might disagree that humans need to be kept less populated and away from various landmasses, but there are a lot of other living things, and Werewolf seems to be an awful lot about intrinsic rights to existence, so there's no reason that human life is more necessary than other forms of life. That incredibly broad scale is closer to the one on which Gaia would operate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T15:15:10-08:00","id":1051706,"title":"","content":"Exactly. To the Fera, it would be worth killing millions of people in Asia who are trying to develop tiger habitat or pouch tiger penile bones because tigers have as much right to exist as humans. The same perspective could be applied in Africa, Australia, Europe, North America, South America, etc. While they might regret killing millions of humans, humans are millions of times more common than wild tigers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T03:47:14-08:00","id":1052484,"title":"","content":"Gaia is some bullshit. The Ratkin are a thing. Their task is literally to prune humanity using pestilence. Same goes for the Werehyenas, whose job is literally the most ableist thing ever; they kill the weak to keep 'the herd' strong. Oh, but they don't kill those under a year old. Great, good to know that those with congenital heart defects in Africa are 100% safe until they're 366 days old.<br /> <br /> RAW, Gaia is basically a Fascist Utilitarian monster who has no place representing the will of the Earth. Also, if you read the origin of the Werefoxes she comes across as an angry bitch who enslaves (can't think of a better word for it, but enslaves is the wrong word) an entire species for basically no reason; she practically admits that there is no purpose to making the foxes into a Fera line.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the War of Rage was pointed in the wrong direction. The Wolves should have obliterated the Hyenas and the Rats.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay now I want to play a Kinfolk who realises that Gaia worship is bullshit, and becomes a Skin Dancer to spite her, going on to start a group whose sole aim is the eradication of Fera whose given task doesn't line up with humanitarianism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-21-2017, 06:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T06:48:08-08:00","id":1052540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052484#post1052484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> RAW, Gaia is basically a Fascist Utilitarian monster who has no place representing the will of the Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a very odd (imo) view of Werewolf and Gaia.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T07:01:10-08:00","id":1052546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052484#post1052484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaia is some bullshit. The Ratkin are a thing. Their task is literally to prune humanity using pestilence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, because there are living things other than humans around. They also need space, so humans crowding them out would be bad. Also, they stypically start by eating excess food stores, rather than with death plagues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same goes for the Werehyenas, whose job is literally the most ableist thing ever; they kill the weak to keep 'the herd' strong. Oh, but they don't kill those under a year old. Great, good to know that those with congenital heart defects in Africa are 100% safe until they're 366 days old. </div> </div> </div>Their purpose in 1e, 2e, and W20 is odd, because it's basically to do what wild predators do anyway - the narration of the Ajaba section of W20 CB dresses it up, but they're basically just taking down anything that they can to acquire food, and one can't ever really fault wild predators for taking what they can get. Note that in Revised, they were more like the Garou in a different location.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> RAW, Gaia is basically a Fascist Utilitarian monster who has no place representing the will of the Earth. </div> </div> </div>Gaia's nature is to grow monsters as the solution to problems. Also, Gaia is larger than you're thinking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if you read the origin of the Werefoxes she comes across as an angry bitch who enslaves (can't think of a better word for it, but enslaves is the wrong word) an entire species for basically no reason; she practically admits that there is no purpose to making the foxes into a Fera line. </div> </div> </div>You're taking what a fox said at face value? (closes eyes, grins extra-wide)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, the War of Rage was pointed in the wrong direction. The Wolves should have obliterated the Hyenas and the Rats. </div> </div> </div>The Wars of Rage were never Her intention to begin with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: Okay now I want to play a Kinfolk who realises that Gaia worship </div> </div> </div>Again, it's not actually worship, and no one really pays Chiminage directly to Gaia, because She's huge and what the hell are you going to do or offer to influence that? Reverence is given, rites are performed, and the closest that most werewolves get to Gaia is to have a good relationship with one of the Incarnae, who intercede more directly on their behalf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> is bullshit, and becomes a Skin Dancer to spite her, going on to start a group whose sole aim is the eradication of Fera whose given task doesn't line up with humanitarianism. </div> </div> </div>You seem to be missing the essential point. I iterated it on the first comment of this post; why should humans get to dictate how the world should be or what's worthy of existing? The answer for Werewolf is &quot;they shouldn't, and things have ended up terrible for it.&quot;. Humans determining what should exist only gets you things that are beneficial to a short-sighted humanity with only its interest in mind. Then, by and large, they'll skip on everything and leave them to die, or make a grievous miscalculation and fuck up royally in the choosing, because they haven't had billions of years to figure out life.<br /> <br /> Of course, those characters can and do still exist. They're just not going to be portrayed in the right, even by standards outside the game, because they're still advocating genocide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T07:04:44-08:00","id":1052547,"title":"","content":"I would say an incorrect and twisted view. Yes, Nature is not nice and kind, so what? The weak die in the animal world so that the species can continue without suffering. <br /> <br /> In the case of the Ratkin, they killed with disease because humans were unwilling to regulate their own reproduction (and before people start claiming that it was impossible before the 20th century, humans have been using abortificants since prehistoric times to terminate pregnancies). In the case of the Ajaba, they killed the weak to spare the loved ones the sin of killing their own (it was better to grieve the death of a loved one at the jaws of a predator than to bear the guilt of being a kin-slayer). While we are natural sympathetic to humans, Gaia (and the Fera) have to preserve the entire biosphere, so humans are going to be targeted if their actions will destroy the biosphere (which would also destroy humanity).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T10:49:26-08:00","id":1052633,"title":"","content":"If you take the lore of the fera and their roles at face value and assume that it's all 100 percent true (doubtful, even in universe) they're just about OK.<br /> <br /> Now imagine you discover fera &quot;IRL&quot;. They're horrific. Creatures created to kill humans aren't something that should exist. From any outside perspective, (a portion of) the shape changers are murderous death cults. Only if the WtA lore as presented is entirely true are they not a murderous death cult. And let's be honest, in the wider WoD there is little chance of it all being true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-21-2017, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T12:24:48-08:00","id":1052689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052546#post1052546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, because there are living things other than humans around. They also need space, so humans crowding them out would be bad. Also, they stypically start by eating excess food stores, rather than with death plagues.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Their purpose in 1e, 2e, and W20 is odd, because it's basically to do what wild predators do anyway - the narration of the Ajaba section of W20 CB dresses it up, but they're basically just taking down anything that they can to acquire food, and one can't ever really fault wild predators for taking what they can get. Note that in Revised, they were more like the Garou in a different location.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Gaia's nature is to grow monsters as the solution to problems. Also, Gaia is larger than you're thinking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You're taking what a fox said at face value? (closes eyes, grins extra-wide)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Wars of Rage were never Her intention to begin with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again, it's not actually worship, and no one really pays Chiminage directly to Gaia, because She's huge and what the hell are you going to do or offer to influence that? Reverence is given, rites are performed, and the closest that most werewolves get to Gaia is to have a good relationship with one of the Incarnae, who intercede more directly on their behalf.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You seem to be missing the essential point. I iterated it on the first comment of this post; why should humans get to dictate how the world should be or what's worthy of existing? The answer for Werewolf is &quot;they shouldn't, and things have ended up terrible for it.&quot;. Humans determining what should exist only gets you things that are beneficial to a short-sighted humanity with only its interest in mind. Then, by and large, they'll skip on everything and leave them to die, or make a grievous miscalculation and fuck up royally in the choosing, because they haven't had billions of years to figure out life.<br /> <br /> Of course, those characters can and do still exist. They're just not going to be portrayed in the right, even by standards outside the game, because they're still advocating genocide.</div> </div> </div> </div>1: This is running under the assumption that the type of balance dictated by the Ratkin is anything approaching rational. They're just people.<br /> <br /> 2: That's not a necessary creation at all. She could have just let Hyenas do their thing. The role of eating sick babies isn't exactly one which needs a Crinos form or Gifts. And she made freaking Healers. Having Healers and Euthanizers in a world of magic is dumb.<br /> <br /> 3: Gaia is a spiritual entity, she can be judged as though she were a person. And making monsters to solve problems isn't innately bad, she just does a terrible job.<br /> <br /> 4: That's a bit of a copout, and it brings all Lore into question since you're saying that the truth of it is variable (which I discuss, just did a post on the W20 board). And I agree, it does vary.<br /> <br /> 5: I was making a side-note, saying that the Garou destroyed the wrong breeds.<br /> <br /> 6: Obeying the commands of a supernatural deity to the point of making it your life sounds like worship to me. They're on the same level as monks and nuns.<br /> <br /> 7: They should get to determine how things are unless you can prove that they shouldn't. And is the word of spirits and the oral tradition of a bunch of monsters proof? I'd say... no. Obviously not. Things have gotten pretty awful with humans ruining the environment. And... that kind of calls Gaia into question again. She made all of these Monsters to keep things normal, to the point of murdering human populations, and it still didn't work. Again, she's an Authoritarian being. Did she ever consider making a Breed whose job is to talk to humans and guide them through wisdom? There are social gifts. But no such breed exists. Gaia, if we take the lore at face value and ignore the humanizing bullshit, is a monster.<br /> <br /> 8: Advocating death to genocidal maniacs. It isn't about wiping out all Ratkin. It's about dismantling the society of Ratkin as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T12:50:06-08:00","id":1052707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052547#post1052547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say an incorrect and twisted view. Yes, Nature is not nice and kind, so what? The weak die in the animal world so that the species can continue without suffering. <br /> <br /> In the case of the Ratkin, they killed with disease because humans were unwilling to regulate their own reproduction (and before people start claiming that it was impossible before the 20th century, humans have been using abortificants since prehistoric times to terminate pregnancies). In the case of the Ajaba, they killed the weak to spare the loved ones the sin of killing their own (it was better to grieve the death of a loved one at the jaws of a predator than to bear the guilt of being a kin-slayer). While we are natural sympathetic to humans, Gaia (and the Fera) have to preserve the entire biosphere, so humans are going to be targeted if their actions will destroy the biosphere (which would also destroy humanity).</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again Aya, as always, you are very good about pointing to the &quot;excess populational contingent&quot;. Yeah, it's easy to say &quot;all life is important, and there are too many humans!&quot;. It's easy to deal with human beings as numbers when we don't see the faces.<br /> <br /> I would like to see YOU with a knife in your hand, calmly explaining to your OWN CHILDREN that the world is overpopulated, and that's why you're doing your part to &quot;fix this problem&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T13:22:31-08:00","id":1052724,"title":"","content":"I love DA: Fae, much more than I love Changelling the Dreaming, because the Fae on that game are inhuman aliens. They have no reason to try to play with human moralities, that makes no sense to them. The Fae in the dark ages are so absolutely monstruous and alien, that the humans will call them <i><u>Fair Folk</u></i>, out of terror (humans fear that cursing them would anger the creatures). The fair folk will curse entire generations of full villages, will kidnap babies, will smash peasants like roaches.<br /> <br /> They are utter monsters.<br /> <br /> The Fae are not <i>evil</i>, because that's not a concept that can fit them. They are alien, their morals are alien, their culture, lifes, existente, they work on a different way. They are NOT a source of active corruption or destruction, however, they lack the empathy that makes us humans.<br /> <br /> But there is no pink-painting them as some kind of &quot;weird heroes&quot;. They aren't heroes (or villains) AT ALL. They are monstruous monsters... And they have no reason AT ALL to care about it.<br /> <br /> But, when you have werewolves with the mind set of &quot;it's ok to be a monster&quot;... Oh please.<br /> <br /> If WtA were a game that portrayed the Garou as inhuman monsters that seek their spiritual purity... Ok, that's a game I would play. Humans are just reproductive bags at best, a plague at worst, and should be used as means for an end, all in the name of Gaia, a monstruous entity that oversees a dog-eat-dog world... Now, that's a game I would play. <br /> <br /> But... Cool hippie-monsters, your friendly monster next door? That's terrible (and untrue).<br /> <br /> I find it funny, why that need to portray the Garou as epic heroes? Why can't we depict them for what they REALLY are - nighmarish inhuman beasts? Why do you guys have that need to make them into heroes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T13:55:07-08:00","id":1052745,"title":"","content":"I always saw werewolves as being mentally equivalent to the main characters from The Walking Dead. Theirs is a harsh and brutal existence, and while they've all adapted to one degree or another, from the perspective of a relatively safe middle class first world existence, they are rather damaged. (I think there is a book called &quot;The Psychology of the Walking Dead&quot; that goes into a great deal of detail on the subject of the characters' mental trauma. Might be interesting Werewolf reading.) And like the Walking Dead protagonists, the Garou are more &quot;doomed heroes&quot; than epic ones. (IMO at least.) When at it's best, the game always had a mood akin to Robert E. Howard's Conan stories, in which no matter how hard people may struggle, civilization is inevitably doomed to fall to the forces of chaos. But still you struggle on.<br /> <br /> (And yes, from the human perspective, the Garou are monsters because almost everything that has improved the human quality of life in the past 100 years or more is usually something that damages the Garou Nation's interests, while at the same time, a huge amount of what the Garou do to combat the Wyrm and other enemies directly or indirectly harms human bystanders. If the PCs close down a factory that's impacting the environment, be it via monkey wrenching violence or by subtle financial maneuvers, you've won a victory against the Wyrm, but at the same time you've put a bunch of innocent people out of work, leaving their kids at risk for malnutrition and a lifetime of poverty and hardship. And odds are, most Garou wouldn't care even if you pointed this fact out to them.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 02-21-2017, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:23:07-08:00","id":1052829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052689#post1052689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1: This is running under the assumption that the type of balance dictated by the Ratkin is anything approaching rational. They're just people.</div> </div> </div> </div>People who are rats, looking to fulfill a deep spiritual purpose as well. People not typically being incredibly rational, especially if they, as most ratfolk do, come from the down and out portions of humanity that have little to lose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2: That's not a necessary creation at all. She could have just let Hyenas do their thing. The role of eating sick babies isn't exactly one which needs a Crinos form or Gifts. And she made freaking Healers. Having Healers and Euthanizers in a world of magic is dumb. </div> </div> </div>All of the ones with different roles, due to some metatextual issues, were in different places. There are limits to how far away the humans can get from the beast, and the only bears in Africa were at the northern end... up until the Romans killed those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3: Gaia is a spiritual entity, she can be judged as though she were a person. And making monsters to solve problems isn't innately bad, she just does a terrible job. </div> </div> </div>Gaia is about as large as any given member of the Triat, if not larger than the lot of them. It's very difficult to make out anything from that distance, and probably a waste of time. Here's your shovel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4: That's a bit of a copout, and it brings all Lore into question since you're saying that the truth of it is variable (which I discuss, just did a post on the W20 board). And I agree, it does vary. </div> </div> </div>No, because i'm not saying that all narrators are excessively on the lying trickster side. Just the cats, coyotes, and foxes. Oh dear, the foxes...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5: I was making a side-note, saying that the Garou destroyed the wrong breeds. </div> </div> </div>And it seemed a bit of a non-sequitur, since we're talking about what some being endorses or doesn't. You, ah, also to be unfamiliar with the entirety of what breeds existed...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6: Obeying the commands of a supernatural deity to the point of making it your life sounds like worship to me. They're on the same level as monks and nuns. </div> </div> </div>No, it's making a payment. That's literally what the term Chiminage means. Also, only Stargazers try to be so isolated in that fashion, and they're in the running with the Red Talons in the least populous tribe competition. I mean, the Ratkin have some religious overtones, but they aren't at all like a monastic order...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7: They should get to determine how things are unless you can prove that they shouldn't. </div> </div> </div>Because humans are easily misled and prone to jumping the gun even with a large amount of information available? And that, by and large at the moment, they seem to be suckers for capitalism, which is incredibly short-sighted? If the first judgment is how much money you can make, go back to the end of the line and forget about moving forward, Peter Weyland. Finally, the entire premise of the game is that humans don't get to be on a pedestal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And is the word of spirits and the oral tradition of a bunch of monsters proof? I'd say... no. Obviously not. Things have gotten pretty awful with humans ruining the environment. And... that kind of calls Gaia into question again. She made all of these Monsters to keep things normal, to the point of murdering human populations, and it still didn't work. </div> </div> </div>Because of the human element, largely. Also, the only ones trimming off humans were supposed to be the rats, and they were doing it by very indirect means. Had the wolves not been prideful and considered warriors to be the best and only required beings (which, note above, is a major problem with humanocentric points of view as well), they could have simply assisted the rats and not caused such a monumental fuckup.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, she's an Authoritarian being. </div> </div> </div>That's like the most hands-off version of authoritarianism that exists, if you can even call it that. Keep in mind she only gave vague purposed to a bunch of beings and then wasn't heard from again for some time, if at all. Even lower-order beings directly connected to her, such as Sea, think on geologic time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did she ever consider making a Breed whose job is to talk to humans and guide them through wisdom? </div> </div> </div>The Apis. The Garou killed them. Also, the Mokole tried to make wise beings from out of primates. It didn't work and the Garou - who are, like more modern Mokole, descended from said primates - almost killed them, with only one quarter or so not facing death from that particular conflict (it was trying to make war with Yama Kings right in hell that nearly killed them instead).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 8: Advocating death to genocidal maniacs. It isn't about wiping out all Ratkin. It's about dismantling the society of Ratkin as is. </div> </div> </div>Wait, weren't we talking about Garou in that point? Ratkin are not at all into reverential social constructs, as they often border on anarchic. You certainly aren't going to get very many of them leading Gaia worship services over the split message of the Rat totem, half of which is the kind and nurturing Mother Rat who helps homeless survive among humanity, the other half being the Rat God, which is a spirit of apocalyptic fervor who sends messages of chaos, destruction, and madness to promote upheaval of the current order of the world.<br /> <br /> Simply put, people seem to be very confused about what Gaia does and doesn't endorse. The problems with the Garou were meant to be their own doing, and the consequences they face are the punishment for going on short-sighted rampages. You're going to want to look way further down on the spiritual chain for responsibility, there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:51:25-08:00","id":1052860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052724#post1052724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But, when you have werewolves with the mind set of &quot;it's ok to be a monster&quot;... Oh please.<br /> <br /> If WtA were a game that portrayed the Garou as inhuman monsters that seek their spiritual purity... Ok, that's a game I would play. Humans are just reproductive bags at best, a plague at worst, and should be used as means for an end, all in the name of Gaia, a monstruous entity that oversees a dog-eat-dog world... Now, that's a game I would play.<br /> <br /> But... Cool hippie-monsters, your friendly monster next door? That's terrible (and untrue).<br /> <br /> I find it funny, why that need to portray the Garou as epic heroes? Why can't we depict them for what they REALLY are - nighmarish inhuman beasts? Why do you guys have that need to make them into heroes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoever said that they were hippies? They have Rage. An attempt to be a hippie would end in blood and guts. They are epic heroes, though; I think you'll find that an epic hero tends to not be very nice, even among humans, since they've traditionally risen to success from fucking over their enemies in grand fashion.<br /> <br /> Also, it's quite debatable if Gaia oversees anything in a traditional manner, and even then, the Triat does this more directly. And the Triat is not exactly nice, since one member tied the other one up and he's trying to break out in a process that's wrecking the whole place, and the other remaining member was locked out of the room and is trying to seep back in like a goo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:58:04-08:00","id":1052866,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> The Apis helped humans find the right mates. If you almost dislocated your shoulder with that stretch, be more careful in the future.<br /> <br /> I'm fully aware of who was wiped out during the War of Rage, thank you.<br /> <br /> The Renown and Gift systems force people to behave a specific way to grow more powerful. Gaia's whole system of spiritual ascendance is a mystically enforced form of authoritarianism. The Renown System is mediated by the ST (and I'm uneasy with a &quot;this is the right choice&quot; system for advancement, but I understand that it's the best way to do it and a key feature of Werewolf), but it originates with the task given by Gaia to the species. She doesn't need to be a hands-on authoritarian, it's a system.<br /> <br /> Basically Gaia, if she has the goals she is supposed to have, should have created something like the Ananasi. Instead she made a group of fragile individuals with specialist jobs, put them in nonsensical locations while their jobs are global, and left them with Wolfy cousins with &quot;gg no re&quot; combat abilities and hair triggers for Frenzy. Gaia, as a person, has zero forsight and the least careful use of power ever. She's the spirit of the world, and she could have done a far better job, if we take the lore at face value.<br /> <br /> It's not 100% relevant to me, since I reconcile all of this by thinking that Gaia simply cannot exist as the Fera present her and the lore presents her. If she did, things would be different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:01:29-08:00","id":1052910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052866#post1052866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> The Apis helped humans find the right mates. If you almost dislocated your shoulder with that stretch, be more careful in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were also the spiritual guides. W20 CB page 231, the first complete paragraph notes that they walked among humans fighting spiritual corruption and advising traditions of spirituality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Renown and Gift systems force people to behave a specific way to grow more powerful. Gaia's whole system of spiritual ascendance is a mystically enforced form of authoritarianism. </div> </div> </div>Difficulty: the same being set up or aided making the pact for the Gurahl Renown and Rank system, which has one category dedicated entirely to healing and otherwise helping others, and the ones for the other Fera except for the Ananasi and Nagah. Many of these Fera emphasize learning about what they don't know, and all have a system in place to rate how truthful someone is to their own at the very least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Renown System is mediated by the ST (and I'm uneasy with a &quot;this is the right choice&quot; system for advancement, but I understand that it's the best way to do it and a key feature of Werewolf), but it originates with the task given by Gaia to the species. She doesn't need to be a hands-on authoritarian, it's a system. </div> </div> </div>If you take the detailed entries at face value, then they value truth, integrity, art, and insight. Most authoritarian systems tend to value only loyalty to a single figure, and leave things at that; Garou and Fera are asking for much, much more out of someone if they want to be trusted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Basically Gaia, if she has the goals she is supposed to have, should have created something like the Ananasi. </div> </div> </div>Emotionless operatives who are shackled to serve disparate members of the Triat as a desperate gambit against being imprisoned by the Wyrm and Weaver? Because the circumstances are quite different. Also, the Ananasi are generally much more fanatical and single-minded while not being any more resistance to being taken in by the enemy. They put on a good front, but the cold word of the text is that a lot of them are in too deep and don't see anything wrong with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Instead she made a group of fragile individuals with specialist jobs, put them in nonsensical locations </div> </div> </div>How much control did she have when working with her stuff? It's only as much as a certain amount of borrowed, real-world metatext would allow. Why are the bears healers? Because of borrowed real world culture that was likely more than a little distorted (possibly through the lens of Shadowrun; just read the description of its bear totem for shamans). Why are wolves warriors? Because they were working with legends of wolves as ferocious killers and trying to make the game still be about monsters. You didn't really break out of this until some more &quot;out-there&quot; Fera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> while their jobs are global, and left them with Wolfy cousins with &quot;gg no re&quot; combat abilities and hair triggers for Frenzy. Gaia, as a person, has zero forsight and the least careful use of power ever. She's the spirit of the world, and she could have done a far better job, if we take the lore at face value. </div> </div> </div>Bigger than the world, actually. That's why doing tiny things is so difficult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not 100% relevant to me, since I reconcile all of this by thinking that Gaia simply cannot exist as the Fera present her and the lore presents her. If she did, things would be different. </div> </div> </div>Well, she's never presented as omnipotent and omniscient, so if you were expecting an all-powerful protective deity, you're looking in the wrong place. Try nowhere in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:14:00-08:00","id":1052922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052910#post1052910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, she's never presented as omnipotent and omniscient, so if you were expecting an all-powerful protective deity, you're looking in the wrong place. Try nowhere in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>So she is bigger than the earth, goes beyond the Triat... and is too weak to fix things or build sensible systems which function as intended. Seems like she's exactly as powerful or weak as you need her to be for your argument to make sense in any one given moment. I'm not asking for her to be omnipotent, since in that scenario there wouldn't be a game, it would be a slice-of-life about Werewolves sitting by the pool talking about which girls/boys they like.<br /> <br /> And the Ananasi are a singular system of Fera who cover every possible necessary role by delegating within one species, with an effectively delineated control system, hierarchy and sensible delegation, with checks and balances like them sharing one Totem Spirit and them all keeping an eye on eachother. They're a flexible breed and their numbers are ridiculous in terms of both Fera and Kinfolk. On top of all of that, they're the &quot;Best Designed&quot; shape-changers, lacking a Supernatural Bane, lacking Frenzy, and having a huge list of possible Gifts. The Daughter Spirit of the Weaver, who is definitely a lot weaker than Gaia, did a better job of designing a Changing Breed than Gaia, is my overall point there. And they're not perfect, but their whole deal is &quot;hey, maybe the Wyrm isn't an inherently bad thing, maybe it needs PTSD counselling&quot;, something that has occurred to basically nobody else (in significant numbers) for some reason (even the Garou, who literally embody destruction and embrace the Wyrm in their role as Warriors).<br /> <br /> I'm asking for the decisions that Gaia makes as a fictional entity to add up with the way she is presented. If they don't, then it's perfectly fair for someone in or out of universe to say &quot;okay, well then, these discrepancies mean that it's fair to dislike Gaia&quot; or &quot;Gaia can't exist as presented, if she did things would be different&quot;. All I'm saying is that a Changer who decides that the roles given to the breeds are bullshit and that Gaia should have zero say shouldn't be seen as a villain by the 'audience', even if the (basically) cultists who marginalize them do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T18:27:14-08:00","id":1052954,"title":"","content":"So I think it's pretty interesting that you seem to praise Queen Ananasa, while describing (wrongly) Gaia as basically functioning exactly how Ananasa does.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052866#post1052866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Basically Gaia, if she has the goals she is supposed to have</div> </div> </div> </div>Serious question: What goals do you think Gaia is supposed to have?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052866#post1052866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> She's the spirit of the world, and she could have done a far better job, if we take the lore at face value.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since she's dying, yea I suppose she could have done a better job. But that is mostly because of the backstory of the setting to set up the &quot;end of times&quot; Apocalypse . The Garou fucked up in pre-history and they are just now getting to see the ramifications of their actions. Not that any of the current Garou had anything to do with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052866#post1052866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's not 100% relevant to me, since I reconcile all of this by thinking that Gaia simply cannot exist as the Fera present her and the lore presents her. If she did, things would be different.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you reconcile it by ignoring the setting as written. I suppose there is no arguing against that kind of logic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052922#post1052922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So she is bigger than the earth, goes beyond the Triat... and is too weak to fix things or build sensible systems which function as intended. Seems like she's exactly as powerful or weak as you need her to be for your argument to make sense in any one given moment. I'm not asking for her to be omnipotent, since in that scenario there wouldn't be a game, it would be a slice-of-life about Werewolves sitting by the pool talking about which girls/boys they like.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you are faulting the setting for her not being omnipotent? I suppose I don't understand your intent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052922#post1052922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And the Ananasi are a singular system of Fera who cover every possible necessary role by delegating within one species, with an effectively delineated control system, hierarchy and sensible delegation, with checks and balances like them sharing one Totem Spirit and them all keeping an eye on eachother.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except when they don't? Like the Kumo?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052922#post1052922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They're a flexible breed and their numbers are ridiculous in terms of both Fera and Kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're about as numerous as the Garou. Since the Gaoru are presented as having about half the number they need for their tasks, this isn't terribly impressive. I'm not sure why you think they are so numerous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052922#post1052922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On top of all of that, they're the &quot;Best Designed&quot; shape-changers, lacking a Supernatural Bane, lacking Frenzy, and having a huge list of possible Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>And lacking real regeneration. And arguably, free will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052922#post1052922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Daughter Spirit of the Weaver, who is definitely a lot weaker than Gaia, did a better job of designing a Changing Breed than Gaia, is my overall point there.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is obviously a matter of opinion. I certainly disagree with you. The Ananasi are cool. But they aren't any &quot;better&quot; designed than any of the other Breeds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052922#post1052922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And they're not perfect, but their whole deal is &quot;hey, maybe the Wyrm isn't an inherently bad thing, maybe it needs PTSD counselling&quot;,</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ananasi's whole deal is: do what the Queen says because she has a plan and knows better than any one of us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052922#post1052922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> something that has occurred to basically nobody else (in significant numbers) for some reason (even the Garou, who literally embody destruction and embrace the Wyrm in their role as Warriors).</div> </div> </div> </div> Plenty of others have decided the Wyrm isn't &quot;the&quot; enemy. Ratkin as a race (the actual most numerous Changing Breed) combat the Weaver, and only fight the Wyrm if it gets in their way. In any case, in setting, the Wyrm is the entity that's bringing out the Apocalypse. So there is that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T20:59:45-08:00","id":1053022,"title":"","content":"Before agriculture, human populations seemed to be stable at around 6 million (if you use older figures) to 60 million (if you use newer figures based on ecological capacity and genetic analysis). The question becomes how did humans stabilize their populations? Famine was rare when population densities were less than 1 person per square kilometer, disease was even rare because the low population density and lack of domesticated animals reduced disease to practically nothing (see the Americas and Australia for examples of practically no diseases before European colonization). War did not seem to exist (despite rare evidence of incidental interpersonal violence). In real life, human populations were probably kept under control with a combination of highly athletic lifestyles, extremely low carbohydrate diets, and (probably) near suicidal levels of adventurism (which can be seen today in modern extreme sports). In cWoD, the Garou and Ratkin probably did not have to do much to keep populations down until the advent of agriculture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T04:32:44-08:00","id":1053129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1053022#post1053022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before agriculture, human populations seemed to be stable at around 6 million (if you use older figures) to 60 million (if you use newer figures based on ecological capacity and genetic analysis). The question becomes how did humans stabilize their populations? Famine was rare when population densities were less than 1 person per square kilometer, disease was even rare because the low population density and lack of domesticated animals reduced disease to practically nothing (see the Americas and Australia for examples of practically no diseases before European colonization). War did not seem to exist (despite rare evidence of incidental interpersonal violence). In real life, human populations were probably kept under control with a combination of highly athletic lifestyles, extremely low carbohydrate diets, and (probably) near suicidal levels of adventurism (which can be seen today in modern extreme sports). In cWoD, the Garou and Ratkin probably did not have to do much to keep populations down until the advent of agriculture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, what a wounderful delight... Life should've been a Nirvana in the caves... Maybe that's why life expectancy were about 35 years... Yep, it should've been a divine existence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T05:40:47-08:00","id":1053147,"title":"","content":"It was an existence in balance with nature, which is the focus of the Fera, rather than a world drowning in sewage, which seems to be the result of ever growing human populations. Whether or not the methods of the Fera are appropriate, the population of humanity on Earth cannot grow forever. Eventually, the biosphere collapses and everything, including humanity, dies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:32:38-08:00","id":1053195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1053129#post1053129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow, what a wounderful delight... Life should've been a Nirvana in the caves... Maybe that's why life expectancy were about 35 years... Yep, it should've been a divine existence</div> </div> </div> </div>Statistical nitpick: it was only an early death if you aggregated child mortality with adult mortality, which is not a realistic outcome or expression of numbers. Anyone who made it to adulthood actually managed to live about as long as most people live today... which might not be all that long. People can die young from no apparent cause, even today, or even die in spite of being treated for a condition that was worsened through sedentary life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:56:26-08:00","id":1053211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052954#post1052954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I think it's pretty interesting that you seem to praise Queen Ananasa, while describing (wrongly) Gaia as basically functioning exactly how Ananasa does.<br /> <br /> Serious question: What goals do you think Gaia is supposed to have?<br /> <br /> <br /> Since she's dying, yea I suppose she could have done a better job. But that is mostly because of the backstory of the setting to set up the &quot;end of times&quot; Apocalypse . The Garou fucked up in pre-history and they are just now getting to see the ramifications of their actions. Not that any of the current Garou had anything to do with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> So you reconcile it by ignoring the setting as written. I suppose there is no arguing against that kind of logic.<br /> <br /> <br /> But you are faulting the setting for her not being omnipotent? I suppose I don't understand your intent.<br /> <br /> <br /> Except when they don't? Like the Kumo?<br /> <br /> <br /> They're about as numerous as the Garou. Since the Gaoru are presented as having about half the number they need for their tasks, this isn't terribly impressive. I'm not sure why you think they are so numerous.<br /> <br /> <br /> And lacking real regeneration. And arguably, free will.<br /> <br /> This is obviously a matter of opinion. I certainly disagree with you. The Ananasi are cool. But they aren't any &quot;better&quot; designed than any of the other Breeds.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Ananasi's whole deal is: do what the Queen says because she has a plan and knows better than any one of us.<br /> <br /> Plenty of others have decided the Wyrm isn't &quot;the&quot; enemy. Ratkin as a race (the actual most numerous Changing Breed) combat the Weaver, and only fight the Wyrm if it gets in their way. In any case, in setting, the Wyrm is the entity that's bringing out the Apocalypse. So there is that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1: I'm saying that Ananasa seems to have a coherent goal, while Gaia is all over the place.<br /> <br /> 1.5: Her goal is a balanced biosphere and a stable existence of the diversity of the earth, balance in the umbral wilds and all of her children doing their proper jobs and getting along. Ideal end-game would be something like the Beast Courts, globally, with the world being in a tranquil and primordial state. Obviously she HAS to fail for WTA to be a thing. Please can she fail in realistic and understandable ways, not &quot;whoops, I guess the angry pack-hunting bastards killed all of the others, maybe I should have taken steps to stop that or make it less likely&quot;.<br /> <br /> 2: That's cool, and I'm happy with the game being a &quot;Gaia is dying&quot; setting, but the set-up for that needs to make sense and she needs to have made realistic mistakes or been ruined in realistic ways. For example, it could be as simple as &quot;she tried to comfort and heal the Wyrm after it was driven mad, but it lashed out at her and struck a blow of pure madness that she could never heal. Her power sapped, she retreated more and more into the umbra, giving less and less guidance to her children, who grew more and more discontented with their brothers and sisters, until one day the Rage could not be contained...&quot;. Like seriously, that's all it would take.<br /> <br /> 3: I reconcile it by saying that the setting's lore, as presented, cannot be the whole story, or must have inaccuracies. Gaia, as presented, would have done a better job delineating the roles of the Breeds and ensuring that they wouldn't implode on eachother.<br /> <br /> 4: I'm faulting her for having made mistakes in her Designs which are patently idiotic, and the setting giving no reason for this happening. You can hand-wave mistakes easily and give lore which supports why they were necessary. I'm not an expert on the Werewolf lore, if there's good reasons for her mistakes then please inform me of them.<br /> <br /> 5: The Kumo are a small faction of Ananasi and they continue to exist because the Queen can't see any reason to hunt them down. Obviously they're not stopping her plans from working. Spiders get everywhere, do you think destroying their rogue wannabe-god cousins would be hard? And you can't compare the Kumo being a thing to the BSDs and the War of Rage being a thing.<br /> <br /> 5.5: The spider-kin are numerous to the point where they can't be counted. And the umbral realms are stuffed full of them too. Ratkin have a similar deal going, yes, and the Garou have the most active out-and-about visible kinfolk.<br /> <br /> 6: Eh, their powers kind of put them out of harms way. A level 3 gift (IIRC) can make a web the size of a football field with Strength 8 restriction, something along those lines. And they're spiders. Spiders don't charge roaring into combat. If any breed doesn't need regeneration, it's them. Plus healing with blood isn't too bad, they can summon insects to eat to restore blood basically for free. As for Free Will, they clearly have it. They just have their Queen breathing down their necks and telling them what not to do and what they must do. Beyond those imperatives they have free will. One of them spends her spare time luring in child molesters to eat, for example, and I doubt the Queen really gives a shit. Plus Blood is a great substitute for Rage in my opinion, and having no Rage to invest freebies or EXP in means that they can max out Gnosis much more easily. And remember that literally (well, almost) any building in the world can be infiltrated by a spider which can easily be kinfolk. And we have the Crawlerling form which takes Indestructable up to 11, even if it has risks.<br /> <br /> 7: That is a matter of opinion, I agree, but the lack of bane and the huge list of potential gifts is quite a big deal. Pick any one Breed and try and make them carry out the role of every Breed. IMO the Ananasi are the only ones who come close, with the Garou having so many tribes it's a bit trickier but I'm guessing that they could do it too.<br /> <br /> 8: And their Queen is an ancient supernatural entity whose whole deal is knowing the right threads to pull on. She's exactly as Right as the ST wants her to be, sure, but she's certainly no dullard.<br /> <br /> 9: But no one else is actively trying to restore sanity to the Wyrm or the Weaver, correct? The Ananasi are born of the Weaver, and even they realise she's gone too far. They actively accept that the Triat needs to be balanced, despite being infinitely stronger in a world where the Weaver runs rampant. And you could easily argue that the Ratkin's efforts to undermine the Weaver are allowed to continue by the Ananasi since it's part of their designs, far easier to let them do some of the work on that front. That's ST caveat however, and it's dumb to say &quot;this splat is actually secretly controlling this splat, you suckers&quot; unless you have a very good story backing it up and don't make one of them look like total chumps (I'm looking at you, Dirty Secrets).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T08:09:11-08:00","id":1053218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1053211#post1053211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1: I'm saying that Ananasa seems to have a coherent goal, while Gaia is all over the place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Gaia is literally all over the place. She's the soul of the place. Eventually, the place has to do something on its own, which means the living things within it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> 5: The Kumo are a small faction of Ananasi and they continue to exist because the Queen can't see any reason to hunt them down. Obviously they're not stopping her plans from working. Spiders get everywhere, do you think destroying their rogue wannabe-god cousins would be hard? And you can't compare the Kumo being a thing to the BSDs and the War of Rage being a thing. </div> </div> </div>The Kumo aren't the only ones; there's also one in the W20 Book of the Wyrm, and the Ananasi also mentions that Ananasa doesn't have nearly as much control as she would like to have. Plenty of hers fall to the temptation of the Wyrm or end up being clarified and returning as Drones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7: That is a matter of opinion, I agree, but the lack of bane and the huge list of potential gifts is quite a big deal. Pick any one Breed and try and make them carry out the role of every Breed. IMO the Ananasi are the only ones who come close, with the Garou having so many tribes it's a bit trickier but I'm guessing that they could do it too. </div> </div> </div>The Ananasi are extremely fragile in comparison to all the other changers. No Rage means no chance to recover from a killing blow on the spot, or spontaneously being able to just throw down. No regeneration means that injuries, diseases and toxins take a lot more out of them. And sure, you can change into a swarm of spiders and try to get away, but the enemy also knows that you don't have the Master of Fire Gift, not that it would help. In the rare event that someone manages to deploy BC weapons against them, they also won't shrug it off like most other changers; they will die, and even faster if they try to get away as a swarm of spiders. Also, often times, their ace in the hole leaves them missing a massive amount of memory because someone got lucky and offed the controller spiders instead of just drones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 8: And their Queen is an ancient supernatural entity whose whole deal is knowing the right threads to pull on. She's exactly as Right as the ST wants her to be, sure, but she's certainly no dullard. </div> </div> </div>Who is also trapped and unable to do very much at all. In fact, she's pretty much being held to blackmail the Ananasi. With a much larger, cosmically-sized being, this isn't something that happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 9: But no one else is actively trying to restore sanity to the Wyrm or the Weaver, correct? The Ananasi are born of the Weaver, and even they realise she's gone too far. They actively accept that the Triat needs to be balanced, despite being infinitely stronger in a world where the Weaver runs rampant. And you could easily argue that the Ratkin's efforts to undermine the Weaver are allowed to continue by the Ananasi since it's part of their designs, far easier to let them do some of the work on that front. That's ST caveat however, and it's dumb to say &quot;this splat is actually secretly controlling this splat, you suckers&quot; unless you have a very good story backing it up and don't make one of them look like total chumps (I'm looking at you, Dirty Secrets). </div> </div> </div>It's supposed to be the new wave of the future for that to be on the agenda. W20 presented the Garou, and then the Fera, as having eaten a lot of shit in the past, but also that they're getting together to make a difference, finally. There was a huge, full-color comic about the Eighth Sign of the Phoenix in the W20 core that I think is supposed to inform a lot of differences between it and fatalistic presentations of the game. All of the terrible shit was a prelude to explain why everything is in a sorry state; now, the player characters can do something about it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T08:16:53-08:00","id":1053221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1053195#post1053195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Statistical nitpick: it was only an early death if you aggregated child mortality with adult mortality, which is not a realistic outcome or expression of numbers. Anyone who made it to adulthood actually managed to live about as long as most people live today... which might not be all that long. People can die young from no apparent cause, even today, or even die in spite of being treated for a condition that was worsened through sedentary life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, throughout history, it was actually fairly common for people to live into their sixties or seventies if they were not killed off by a brand new disease (like the Black Plague during the 14th century in Europe) or a war. Child mortality was high, the majority of children died before they reached puberty, but there are a lot of reasons for that beyond infectious diseases. Genetic disorders probably killed off a lot of children between birth and puberty and, while it was tragic, it did mean that the human species was naturally weeding out the genetic disorders before they could pass on their weaknesses to the next generation. There are hundreds to thousands of genetic disorders that are not immediately fatal to children when they are born that will kill them off over time without modern medicine, and the majority of them are just caused by random damage to the chromosomes due to errors in cell replication during the earliest days of a pregnancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T08:19:56-08:00","id":1053224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1053221#post1053221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, throughout history, it was actually fairly common for people to live into their sixties or seventies if they were not killed off by a brand new disease (like the Black Plague during the 14th century in Europe) or a war. Child mortality was high, the majority of children died before they reached puberty, but there are a lot of reasons for that beyond infectious diseases. Genetic disorders probably killed off a lot of children between birth and puberty...</div> </div> </div> </div>You should have stopped here. Eugenics doesn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T09:26:41-08:00","id":1053265,"title":"","content":"No one is advocating eugenics. It is just a reality that nature selects against the spread of genetic disorders caused by random mutations. It is called evolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T09:28:48-08:00","id":1053268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1053265#post1053265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one is advocating eugenics. It is just a reality that nature selects against the spread of genetic disorders caused by random mutations. It is called evolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back mutation rates make that less likely, as various traits can just crop up out of the blue. Also, the voice in which one describes a selection pressure matters; glowing praise is basically eugenics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T04:51:27-07:00","id":1075436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1053224#post1053224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You should have stopped here. Eugenics doesn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Selective breeding<br /> gene engineering<br /> hybridization<br /> <br /> so when we call it by another name and do it to some other species it works, right? But as soon as it's done to someone who's DNA differs by 0.1% instead of 1% it's revolting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 04-30-2017, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T04:53:17-07:00","id":1075437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1052724#post1052724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there is no pink-painting them as some kind of &quot;weird heroes&quot;. They aren't heroes (or villains) AT ALL. They are monstruous monsters... And they have no reason AT ALL to care about it.<br /> <br /> But, when you have werewolves with the mind set of &quot;it's ok to be a monster&quot;... Oh please.<br /> <br /> If WtA were a game that portrayed the Garou as inhuman monsters that seek their spiritual purity... Ok, that's a game I would play. Humans are just reproductive bags at best, a plague at worst, and should be used as means for an end, all in the name of Gaia, a monstruous entity that oversees a dog-eat-dog world... Now, that's a game I would play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the target group has a mentality that wants to play the 'Heroes'? besides such a thing would attract too much vocal attacks over the net, decreasing the sales. <br /> <br /> Try BSD, or move to Beast the Primordial. They explicitly did away with Built-in morality there. Game even punishes you for being too nice and killing adds+4 to feeding roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T07:19:44-07:00","id":1075466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1075436#post1075436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Selective breeding<br /> gene engineering<br /> hybridization<br /> <br /> so when we call it by another name and do it to some other species it works, right? But as soon as it's done to someone who's DNA differs by 0.1% instead of 1% it's revolting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every genome is equivalent. Humans tend to lack the neutral network of genes that many domesticated animals possess. There are a number of genes that, when deactivated, don't result in immediately catastrophic reactions. The human genome really can't take the kind of stresses that humans put other animals under with selective breeding; just look as the Hapsburgs, particularly Charles II of Spain. You'd need to use some fantastic gene modding to get good results out of that for humans, and by fantastic, I mean appearing in a work of fantasy, like, say, BattleTech, which is also influenced by the creators not really knowing or caring much about genetics in the first place (there's a common slip-up about believing that only recessive genes cause deleterious effects that's presence among some of the material).<br /> <br /> Also, I find the process by which we got white tigers to be quite weird and disturbing, and do you think that doesn't fire my want to shoot down this concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T07:57:20-07:00","id":1075480,"title":"","content":"Well, the reason why selective breeding for animals and plants work is that we ruthlessly destroy anything with undesirable genes, which we are unwilling to do with humans. Even so, most purebred strains have a list of genetic disorders as long as your arm, they are just tolerated because they do not interfere with the function of the strain. While we all selectively breed with specific mates, we are usually interested in the whole package rather than individual traits.<br /> <br /> It is not that you cannot selectively breed humans, it is just that we are unwilling to weed out people with undesirable characteristics from the gene pool because we are ethical. Anyway, I doubt most of us would be comfortable with the tradeoffs required for genetic optimization. The idea of selectively breeding a strain of beautiful humans with insatiable sexual appetites as a caste of dedicated sex workers is squicky, especially if their average IQ is 80, if they develop diabetes if they are allowed to eat a carb rich diet, and if all of them develop severe Parkinson's by the time they are forty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T03:38:19-07:00","id":1076397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1075480#post1075480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the reason why selective breeding for animals and plants work is that we ruthlessly destroy anything with undesirable genes, which we are unwilling to do with humans. Even so, most purebred strains have a list of genetic disorders as long as your arm, they are just tolerated because they do not interfere with the function of the strain. While we all selectively breed with specific mates, we are usually interested in the whole package rather than individual traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>this. I looked a bit into it and it's actually worse then what Aya Tari says. <br /> <br /> also, wanted to add that our handling of the world and ourselves is very short sighted and will come to bite us in the ass very soon. What I wanted to say is that humans aren't some chosen race of the masters of the planet, driving Earth to better future through beneficient leadership. We are greedy, cowardly animals with overdeveloped intelligence. there is actually little difference between humans and other animals in DNA or psychology. humans basically act as invasive species on global scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T06:13:45-07:00","id":1076434,"title":"","content":"Pretty much. What is sad is that we possess the foresight and intellect to be something better, but we choose not to as a group. Rather than make the right choices, we make the easy choices, and the easy choices are usually bad choices. In effect, we are worse than animals because we have the ability to be better than animals, if you get what I am saying. That being said we are animals, and we are omnivores, so we are evolved to make certain types of choices, but there are right choices and bad choices even under those conditions (we can choose to treat the animals we slaughter more humanely, so they do not feel fear or pain before their moment of death).<br /> <br /> One of the examples of this comes from genetic engineering. Monsanto decided that a fish gene that protects fish from freezing would be wonderful to add to tomatoes. You can read the story here (<a href=\"http://www.motherearthnews.com/real-food/adding-a-fish-gene-into-tomatoes-zmaz00amzgoe\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.motherearthnews.com/real-...s-zmaz00amzgoe</a>). While that was an easy problem to address, let the new breed go extinct, there are millions of examples throughout the last twenty years of people going for the easy choice rather than the right choice. In many ways, modern humans are the dark god of the Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T10:58:50-07:00","id":1085075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1076434#post1076434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much. What is sad is that we possess the foresight and intellect to be something better, but we choose not to as a group. Rather than make the right choices, we make the easy choices, and the easy choices are usually bad choices. In effect, we are worse than animals because we have the ability to be better than animals, if you get what I am saying. That being said we are animals, and we are omnivores, so we are evolved to make certain types of choices, but there are right choices and bad choices even under those conditions (we can choose to treat the animals we slaughter more humanely, so they do not feel fear or pain before their moment of death).</div> </div> </div> </div>Human morality is very debatable. Most of it is clearly delusion, both of others and ourselves. Most would better die then admit it. .<br /> <br /> Look through 'Straw Dogs', 'Lucifer's Principle', etc. Gives interesting viewpoint. They explain it way better then poor old me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 04-28-2017, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T11:11:56-07:00","id":1085081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1050549-my-dark-god-beats-yours-who-is-the-most-evil-one-in-wod?p=1050727#post1050727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Belial is barely on the level of the others in that list. Sure, he's extremely powerful but he's powerful on a level that player characters can hypothetically deal with thim. The others? Not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure. Doesn't he move at the speed of light? And have the ability to split the Earth with a well placed earthquake?<br /> <br /> Edit: On second consideration, I see what you mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 04-29-2017, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name"